==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ɹʌŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-rung.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌŋ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|rng|wrung}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hrung}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hrungō}}. Compare {{cog|got|𐌷𐍂𐌿𐌲𐌲𐌰|t=a staff}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Rungs of ladders and chair (PSF).png|thumb|Rungs of ladders and chair (PSF)]]
# A [[crosspiece]] forming a [[step]] of a [[ladder]]; a [[round]].
# A [[crosspiece]] between [[leg]]s of a [[chair]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1854|author={{w|Nathaniel Hawthorne}}|title={{w|Mosses from an Old Manse}}|chapter=Feathertop: a Moralized Legend|passage=One of its arms was a disabled flail which used to be wielded by Goodman Rigby, before his spouse worried him out of this troublesome world; the other, if I mistake not, was composed of the pudding stick and a broken '''rung''' of a chair, tied loosely together at the elbow.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[position]] in a [[hierarchy]].
#: {{ux|en|the lowest '''rung''' of the society}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|dated}} A [[floor]] [[timber]] in a [[ship]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} One of the [[stake]]s of a [[cart]]; a [[spar]]; a heavy [[staff]].
# {{lb|en|engineering|dated}} One of the [[radial]] [[handle]]s [[project]]ing from the [[rim]] of a [[steering wheel]].
# {{lb|en|engineering|dated}} One of the [[pin]]s or [[trundle]]s of a [[lantern wheel]].

