====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{past participle of|en|ring|nocat=1}} {{qualifier|only in senses related to a bell}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|_|dialectal}} {{en-simple past of|ring}}
#* '''1723''', Charles Walker, ''Memoirs of Sally Salisbury'', VI:
#*: With ecchoing Shouts the vaulted Chamber '''rung''', / ''Belle Chuck'' was now the ''TOAST'' of ev'ry Tongue.
#* {{quote-journal|en|journals=Report of State Officers, Board and Committees to the General ...|page=229|books.google.com/books?id=YHYbAQAAIAAJ|South Carolina. General Assembly|year=1906|passage=Mr. Seibels, in his testimony, said I '''rung''' him up to see about labels. He is very much mistaken. I '''rung''' him up to see about bottles.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Wrigleyville: A Magical History Tour of the Chicago Cubs|page=435|books.google.com/books?isbn=1429904801|author=Peter Golenbock|year=1996|passage=So they '''rung''' him up, and the next day he came to me and wanted to know where that pitch was.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Burning Rainbow Farm: How a Stoner Utopia Went Up in Smoke|page=70|books.google.com/books?isbn=1596919906|author=Dean Kuipers|year=2008|passage="I just '''rung''' him up, told him I was looking for an apartment and some work and got both of them the same day," Moe said.}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of a pig: having a ring through the nose.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1842|title=American Turf Register and Sporting Magazine|volume=13|page=335
|passage={{...}} he passed by his gate with a decided scowl on his furrowed brow, and grunting and growling like a newly '''rung''' pig.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1919|journal=Popular Science|volume=95|issue=4|page=31
|passage=A "'''rung'''" pig is comfortable as long as he confines his food hunt to the surface of the ground. Ringing a pig of ordinary size is easy, but special arrangements must be made for handling the big ones.}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|en|rang|Rang}} and {{m|en|rung}} are incorrect for the past of {{m|en|ring}} in the sense of {{m|en|encircle}}, where {{m|en|ringed}} is used instead.

{{m|en|rung|Rung}} as a simple past is usually considered incorrect.

